FIXED: Clash no longer drops casts when translating GHC Core to Clash Core.
Dropped casts were the root cause of a family of bugs involving newtypes,
type families over newtypes, `unsafeCoerce`d constraint evidence, and
`ghc-typelits-knownnat` evidence: [#760](https://github.com/clash-lang/clash-compiler/issues/760),
[#1927](https://github.com/clash-lang/clash-compiler/issues/1927),
[#2376](https://github.com/clash-lang/clash-compiler/issues/2376),
[#2812](https://github.com/clash-lang/clash-compiler/issues/2812),
[#2882](https://github.com/clash-lang/clash-compiler/issues/2882), and
[#2961](https://github.com/clash-lang/clash-compiler/issues/2961).
The normalizer, compile-time evaluator, and netlist generator have learned to
push casts around (and eliminate them) using the push rules from "System FC
with Explicit Kind Equality" (Weirich et al., ICFP '13).
